            <ArticleTitle>Pediatric wound care and management in the emergency department</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Traumatic wounds and lacerations are common pediatric presenting complaints to emergency departments. Although there is a large body of literature on wound care, many emergency clinicians base management of wounds on theories and techniques that have been passed down, so controversial, conflicting, and unfounded recommendations are prevalent. This issue reviews evidence-based recommendations for wound care and management, including wound cleansing and irrigation, anxiolysis/sedation techniques, closure methods, and post-repair wound care.</AbstractText>
